            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "), and nothing else can run it: not the CLI, chat, the router, the API, another pack, or a project workflow. Inside a pack, a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "workflow:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " child run may launch another entrypoint of the pack by its YAML "
        },
        {
          "insert": "name:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", but not a support workflow, because a child run is dispatch."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-global-workflows-names-a-qualified-n-27": {
      "id": "b-50-global-workflows-names-a-qualified-n-27",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Names.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " A qualified name matches exactly (case-sensitive) and never by suffix or substring, and a project or global workflow that declares an installed name is not loaded. Inside a pack, a reference to a YAML "
        },
        {
          "insert": "name:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " shared by multiple files fails discovery; when the files have distinct public identities, use a qualified identity such as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "acme/review-kit:review",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " to select the intended target. Qualified identities take precedence over colliding authored names. Support identities use the YAML "
        },
        {
          "insert": "name:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", so two support files with the same name also have the same public identity and fail discovery. Rename one support workflow and update its references; qualification cannot distinguish them."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-global-workflows-runs-keep-their-revisi-28": {
      "id": "b-50-global-workflows-runs-keep-their-revisi-28",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Runs keep their revision.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " A run freezes the pack at the commit it started with, and a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "workflow:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " child takes the packs its parent froze. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon plugin update",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " or "
        },
        {
          "insert": "remove",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " affects only runs that start afterwards."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-global-workflows-installed-or-copied-29": {
      "id": "b-50-global-workflows-installed-or-copied-29",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Installed or copied.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " An installed pack is read-only and changes only through "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon plugin update",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". To change one for a single project, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "archon plugin copy <id>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " writes it to "
        },
        {
          "insert": ".archon/workflows/<name>/",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", where it is an ordinary project pack: its workflows run under their own "
        },
        {
          "insert": "name:",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "update",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " no longer touches it."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-50-global-workflows-practical-examples-30": {
